# What must not reach the image, for `docker build -f panel/Dockerfile panel`.
#
# The Dockerfile copies the whole context in one `COPY . .`, and until this file
# existed there was nothing between that and whatever the person building had
# left in panel/. .gitignore does not apply to a build context, so the very
# files it exists to keep out of the repository - a development database, a
# generated signing key, a 130 MB virtualenv - were the files being baked into a
# distributable image.
#
# The secrets are the reason this is not merely a size fix. .dev/data/secret.key
# is the Django signing key `make dev` generates, and .dev/data/db.sqlite3 holds
# the accounts and sessions that went with it. Neither is what the container runs
# on - AWG_PANEL_DATA points at /var/lib/awg-panel, so a fresh key is made on
# first start - but both are a developer's credentials, shipped to whoever pulls
# the image, in a file nothing would ever think to look at.
#
# release.yml's source tarball already excludes this same set. That list and this
# one are the two ways the project hands out a copy of itself, and they should
# keep saying the same thing.

# The virtualenv. 130 MB of the wrong architecture's wheels as often as not, and
# the image builds its own from the locks a few lines above the COPY.
.venv
.lockgen

# Runtime state from `make dev`, `make test` and `make demo`. The signing key and
# the account database live in here.
.dev
.demo
db.sqlite3
staticfiles

# Node's tree, which is 219 MB and which the image has no use for: the UI is
# built before the image is, and only frontend/dist is copied in.
#
# frontend/dist is deliberately NOT listed. It is the built SPA, the Dockerfile
# fails the build without it, and it is the one artifact here that must be
# copied.
**/node_modules

# Caches, and the wheels fetch-wheels.sh downloads for the offline installer -
# the image installs from the locks over the network instead.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
wheels

# Nothing in the image reads these, and a stale one is a misleading thing to
# find inside a container.
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
